{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "1e26e824-7e91-88c7-898c-162adc1dfd4f",
  "created_at": "2025-12-08T11:12:17-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Fernando Medeiros",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Lorraine Medeiros",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T11:08:58-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Lorraine. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T11:09:03-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, good morning. My name is Fernando Medeiros. I am calling about the water at my building. It is at 76 Farewell Street, in the North End."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T11:09:14-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, 76 Farewell Street. Good morning, Mr. Medeiros. What's the water doing?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T11:09:19-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So, the parking lot behind the building, it goes down toward the back door. When it rains hard, all the water comes to the door and stands there. After the nor'easter that ended Saturday, two days ago, the water was inside the entrance. [pause] Ai, que chatice. Very bad."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T11:09:37-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh no. So the lot slopes toward the back entrance and the water pools at the door and came in the hallway?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T11:09:46-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, exactly. Into the entrance, the little hall by the door. I am renting here, so I cannot change the lot. I put towels, but it is not enough. And it is not the first time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T11:10:00-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Has it happened before, then?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T11:10:03-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "My neighbor, the lady next door, she says it happens every big rain. Every one. So it is not only this storm. Somebody should look, no? The city, they should come and see why the water goes there."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T11:10:18-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I understand. Let me make sure I have this right. The parking lot behind 76 Farewell, water runs to the back door, floods the entrance, and your neighbor says it happens with every heavy rain."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T11:10:31-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, that is correct. Every heavy rain."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T11:10:35-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So I want to ask, who do I call to get it checked? Is it you, or is it somebody else? I do not know if the lot is the city or the owner."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T11:10:48-05:00",
      "duration": 21,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good question. If it's a private lot, the drainage on it is usually the property owner's responsibility. But if there's a city storm drain nearby that's blocked or backing up, that's ours, and we can send someone to look at it. I'll put in a request for a crew to check the drains around there."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T11:11:09-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, please. That would be good. I also will tell the landlord, but he does not answer very fast."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T11:11:17-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's fine, tell him too. Is there a storm drain you can see near the lot, or out on Farewell Street?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T11:11:25-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "[pause] There is one on the street, in front, I think. In the back I do not see one. Only the water going to the door."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T11:11:35-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. I'll note no visible drain in the back lot, one on the street out front. And a good number to reach you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T11:11:44-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, it is 401-555-0166."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T11:11:46-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Four-oh-one, five-five-five, oh-one-six-six. Got it. Someone from the department should follow up after they look at it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T11:11:53-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you. I hope they come soon, because more rain is coming this week, they say. Now I must go. I have to find a gift for a white elephant exchange, for a party, and I have no idea what to buy."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T11:12:09-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good luck with that. Thanks for calling, Mr. Medeiros."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T11:12:13-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you very much. Have a good day."
    }
  ],
